#
# Plasma applets are Qt plugins. plasmashell only loads them from directories
# on Qt's plugin search path, which by default is *only*
#     @OBSIDIANNOTE_QT_SYSTEM_PLUGIN_DIR@
# (qtpaths6 --query QT_INSTALL_PLUGINS). This applet is installed user-locally
# into
#     @OBSIDIANNOTE_PLUGIN_ROOT@
# so that directory has to be added to QT_PLUGIN_PATH for the whole session.
#
# systemd's user manager reads every ~/.config/environment.d/*.conf at login
# (systemd-environment-d-generator) and plasma-plasmashell.service inherits the
# result, so this survives logout/reboot without touching any shell rc file.
#
# The ${VAR:+...} form below is expanded by systemd itself: the directory is
# PREPENDED to any pre-existing QT_PLUGIN_PATH instead of clobbering it, and no
# stray ":" is left behind when QT_PLUGIN_PATH was unset.
QT_PLUGIN_PATH=@OBSIDIANNOTE_PLUGIN_ROOT_TEMPLATED@${QT_PLUGIN_PATH:+:${QT_PLUGIN_PATH}}
